			"to": "western-civ/printing-press",
			"why": "Petrucci brought to polyphonic music, in Venice in 1501, the printing from movable metal type that Gutenberg's press had brought to words half a century before."
		},
		{
			"to": "western-civ/gutenberg-bible",
			"why": "Fust and Schöffer, who took over Gutenberg's equipment after the Bible, printed the Mainz Psalter of 1457 with its chant left to be written in by hand, as the Bible's red headings were."
		},
